Z||000003||falconhulk||10-09-2001||08:32 AM||||I sent this exact question to a guy selling these solid covers on ebay.  He assured me they would fit any year fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||10-09-2001||08:39 AM||||The stock '84 solid covers will only work on notchbacks, they are almost perfectly square. <P>I'd think it would be easier to modify or make a set of solid covers out the ones for the fastback.  Never seen it done, would be neat but I'd be concerned about trapping heat. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||10-09-2001||08:54 AM||||Notchback grills are square and flat. Fastback grills are shaped and curved down to meet the body because the decklid is higher. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Smoooooth GT||10-09-2001||09:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Notchback grills are square and flat. Fastback grills are shaped and curved down to meet the body because the decklid is higher. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Orief....  would this trap too much heat??? Like i said I have side and sail scoop's...<BR>Our GT vnt's curve down at the window... the side scoop would cover that so the flat edge would'nt show..??  Can it be done?? Steve<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L V/6<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
