Z||000010||grinthock||10-09-2001||10:37 PM||||The side scoops provide air INLETS, the sail scoops don't do much of anything except cause air to rush down the decklid and less down the trailing edges of the body.<P>The air that goes IN STILL MUST ESCAPE!  YOu need a way to get the air that has entered OUT of the engine bay, this is EXACTLY what those panels DO!  I removed the screens in mine for better airflow infact! So did slammedfiero.<P>You need those vents.   Removing them or putting on solid panels would be foolish.  Don't.  Those are the primary cooling VENTS for the engine bay.  while your other scoops are air inlets.<P><BR>Hope that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tigger||10-09-2001||10:49 PM||||Not really modify them, but smooth a set out, mock them up, make a master, then make fiberglass smoothies.<P>For appearance they would look good, but you'd lose a lot of functionality.  A Mustang scoop would help, but not sure if enough.<P>I guess the quick way would be to do an experiment.  Take some ducktape (handyman secret weapon) and tape up the vents.  Drive the car around the block and see what the temp guage does.||||reg||1
Z||000012||ginoferrari||10-09-2001||10:51 PM||||I put vented panels on my 84 SC so it has vents all the way across now. It seens to have made the car run a little cooler. I wanted all the air flow I could get through the engine compartment.||||reg||9
